# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Kisung Kang et al. (2025). Accelerating the training and improving the reliability of machine-learned interatomic potentials for strongly anharmonic materials through active learning.
#   Physical Review Materials. doi:10.1103/physrevmaterials.9.063801  arXiv:2409.11808v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2409.11808v1 (sha256 500799a2ce0b4f29...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 445 (Training/reliability). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/kang2025accelerating.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: NequIP models (rmax 5 A, lmax 3, 32 features, four
# layers, eight radial basis functions; float64) trained for 112 bulk
# materials from the aiMD data of an earlier anharmonicity study (FHI-aims
# PBEsol), and the ALmoMD active-learning workflow (ensemble of six
# models; acquisition by energy, maximum-force or anharmonicity
# uncertainty), with CuI and AgGaSe2 as worked cases. All errors are
# shown in histograms or curves (Figs. 4, 8, 11); phonon lifetimes,
# NEB paths and thermal conductivities are properties.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
