###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Energy and force MAEs for the 112 materials are shown only as histograms (Fig. 4), and the convergence of test MAEs with training size for CuI and AgGaSe2 only as curves (Figs. 8, 11; the text states only that MAEs below 0.5 meV/atom are acceptable).
# - The per-material models are summarised as one run because the paper does not list them individually. Minimum-energy paths, defect formation in MD, phonon lifetimes and thermal conductivities are properties.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/kang2025accelerating.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.
